## Talk to it

Any Agent Protocol client works — there is no skein-specific SDK:

```ts
import { Client } from "@langchain/langgraph-sdk";

const client = new Client({ apiUrl: "http://localhost:2024" });
const thread = await client.threads.create();
const answer = await client.runs.wait(thread.thread_id, "echo", {
  input: { messages: [{ role: "user", content: "hello" }] },
});
```

The same server backs the `useStream` React hook — point it at the URL and you have a streaming chat
UI. See [Frontend SDKs](https://skein-js.github.io/skein-js/react-sdk).

## Ship it

`skein build` bundles your graphs to plain JavaScript in `.skein/build`; `skein start` serves that
bundle with no TypeScript toolchain in the loop. That pair is exactly what the production image runs.

```bash
<%= runServices %>   # Postgres + Redis
# then uncomment POSTGRES_URI and REDIS_URI in .env
<%= runBuild %>
<%= runStart %>
```

`skein start` is durable-only: it expects `POSTGRES_URI` and `REDIS_URI`, because that is what makes
runs survive a restart and lets you run more than one instance. For a container instead,
`npx skein up` brings up the whole stack, and `npx skein build` (without `--artifact-only`) produces
the image.

